.TH GFXTUNE\-RUN 1 2026-11-07 "gfxtune @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gfxtune\-run \- start a Steam game with its gfxtune settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gfxtune\-run
.I command
.RI [ argument ...]
.PP
In a game's Steam launch options:
.B gfxtune\-run %command%
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gfxtune\-run
reads the settings
.BR gfxtune (1)
keeps for all games and for the game Steam is starting (found from
.BR SteamAppId ),
sets the matching options of Mesa, DXVK, VKD3D\-Proton and Proton as
environment variables, starts gamescope, GameMode or MangoHud around the
game where they are switched on, and then replaces itself with the game.
When a filter or performance measuring is on, it asks Vulkan to load
gfxtune's layer into the game, and only that game. When frame generation
is on, it writes lsfg\-vk's settings for the game to
.I ~/.config/gfxtune/lsfg\-vk/APPID/conf.toml
and points lsfg\-vk at that file, provided lsfg\-vk is installed and
Lossless Scaling's frame generation file is where gfxtune last found it.
.PP
Whatever the game's Steam launch options already set wins: a variable they
set, or gamescope, GameMode or MangoHud they start, is left as it is.
What was applied, kept or left out is written to
.IR ~/.config/gfxtune/last\-launch/APPID.ini ,
which the game's page in gfxtune shows.
.PP
Whatever goes wrong, the game still starts: with nothing to do, an unknown
game or a wrapper that cannot start,
.B gfxtune\-run
starts the command unchanged.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SteamAppId
The game Steam is starting; set by Steam.
.B SteamGameId
and
.B STEAM_COMPAT_APP_ID
are read when it is missing.
.TP
.B DISABLE_GFXTUNE_FILTERS=1
Keeps gfxtune's Vulkan layer out of the game whatever its settings say.
.TP
.BR LSFGVK_PROFILE ", " LSFGVK_CONFIG ", " LSFGVK_ENV ", " DISABLE_LSFGVK
lsfg\-vk's own ways of choosing its settings. Set in the game's launch
options, they win over gfxtune's frame generation setting.
.TP
.B QT_LOGGING_RULES="gfxtune.launch.debug=true"
Also prints what was applied, to the game's output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The game's own, since
.B gfxtune\-run
becomes the game. 2 without a command; 127 when the command cannot be started.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gfxtune (1)
